{"id":"n-20261021-o2r0ur","category":"finance","display_title":"Wall Street Gains and Housing Slump","display_title_he":"עליות בוול סטריט ושפל בשוק הדיור","short_summary":"Wall Street closed higher despite economic uncertainty, while the US housing market faced a historic slump due to rising mortgage rates.","english_level":"C1","words":428,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Wall_west_of_Gains_Law_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1508936.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"Andrew Curtis · CC BY-SA 2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wall_west_of_Gains_Law_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1508936.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001560080","title":"וול סטריט ננעלה בעליות על רקע ירידת מחירי הנפט ותשואות האג\"ח","published_at":"2026-10-20T20:00:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-20T20:00:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-21T06:14:11.681Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Wall Street managed to close with notable gains as declining oil prices and falling bond yields helped investors temporarily set aside growing anxieties regarding massive capital expenditures in artificial intelligence infrastructure. According to market data, the Nasdaq index finished relatively flat, whereas the Dow Jones Industrial Average climbed by approximately 0.9%, and the S&P 500 advanced by 0.2%. Market sentiment received support from optimism surrounding upcoming corporate earnings reports, helping indices successfully overcome earlier intraday volatility and chip sector fluctuations. Nearly 400 companies within the S&P 500 ultimately rose, erasing earlier losses, while a recovery in semiconductor equities contributed to the broader positive momentum. Brent crude oil settled below $109 per barrel during the session, and discussions regarding potential diplomatic contacts concerning the United States and Iran continued, even though a diplomat noted that reports of a finalized peace agreement were premature.","In corporate developments, General Motors released its third-quarter financial results, surpassing analyst expectations with revenues reaching $50 billion, representing a 2.9% increase compared to the same period last year. The automotive manufacturer reported an adjusted operating income of $4.1 billion, and despite narrowing its full-year earnings guidance range rather than raising it, the company revealed a massive $20 billion share buyback program. Its adjusted earnings per share reached $3.70, beating analyst predictions. Meanwhile, London-listed trading platform provider Plus500 announced its second acquisition within a single week, agreeing to purchase the Brazilian broker Guru to accelerate growth across Latin America, funded entirely from its substantial cash reserves, which stood at $860 million at the end of the first half of the year.","Conversely, the macroeconomic landscape presented stark challenges, particularly within the American housing sector. Data from the National Association of Realtors indicated that pending home sales plummeted in September by 7.3% from the previous month, marking the lowest recorded level since tracking began in 2001 and far exceeding the modest contraction anticipated by surveyed economists. This historic downturn followed a sharp surge in borrowing costs, with the average 30-year fixed mortgage rate climbing toward 7.4% after opening the month lower. Real estate agents and homebuilders reported that elevated financing expenses heavily paralyzed activity, prompting frustrated sellers to reduce asking prices while builders heavily subsidized mortgage rates to attract hesitant buyers amidst rising material and labor costs.","Commodity markets also remained in focus as international benchmark Brent crude hovered near multi-month highs, trading around $109 to $111 per barrel. Geopolitical tensions, including recurring rhetoric regarding sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz and ongoing regional conflicts, continued to influence energy valuations and inflate broader inflationary pressures ahead of upcoming monetary policy decisions by the Federal Reserve, which markets anticipate will maintain interest rates."],"facts":[{"fact":"Wall Street finished trading with gains as oil prices and bond yields declined, while investors set aside concerns regarding massive artificial intelligence investments.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Nasdaq closed unchanged, the Dow Jones rose approximately 0.9%, and the S&P 500 gained 0.2%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"General Motors reported third-quarter revenues of $50 billion, beating analyst expectations, and announced a new $20 billion share buyback program.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"US pending home sales plunged in September to their lowest level since tracking began, driven by a sharp surge in mortgage rates.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Brent crude traded around $109 to $111 per barrel amid geopolitical tensions and concerns surrounding the Strait of Hormuz.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Trading platform provider Plus500 announced the acquisition of Brazilian broker Guru, following its acquisition of US-based Hedge.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Wall Street","lemma":"Wall Street","pos":"noun","he":"וול סטריט","name":true},{"text":"managed","lemma":"manage","pos":"verb","he":"הצליח","name":false},{"text":"to close","lemma":"close","pos":"verb","he":"לסגור","name":false},{"text":"with","lemma":"with","pos":"preposition","he":"עם","name":false},{"text":"notable","lemma":"notable","pos":"adjective","he":"בולט","name":false},{"text":"gains","lemma":"gain","pos":"noun","he":"עליות","name":false},{"text":"as","lemma":"as","pos":"conjunction","he":"כאשר","name":false},{"text":"declining","lemma":"decline","pos":"adjective","he":"יורד","name":false},{"text":"oil","lemma":"oil","pos